  "body": "### What is the expected enhancement?\n\n#841 goes a long way in refactoring the electronic structure stack. However, there are still some aspects left for another PR which I would like to summarize in this issue:\r\n\r\nI would still like to apply the following changes:\r\n- remove the `name` attribute of the `Property` base class (the `PropertiesContainer` handles this consistently via `self.__class__.__name__`\r\n- remove the legacy HDF5 integration from those objects\r\n- properly document that a `Property` at that point just means `SparseLabelOpFactory`\r\n- remove remaining data currently stored on property classes in favor of direct storage on the `ElectronicStructureProblem`:\r\n  - `ElectronicStructureProblem.num_particles: int | tuple[int, int]`\r\n  - `ElectronicStructureProblem.num_spatial_orbitals: int | tuple[int, int]` (generalizes `num_spin_orbitals` to enable non-equal orbital numbers per spin species; we can keep the `num_spin_orbitals` property to return the sum of the spatial ones or twice its value when its an integer)\r\n  - `ElectronicStructureProblem.orbital_occupations`\r\n  - `ElectronicStructureProblem.orbital_occupations_b`\r\n- change `AngularMomentum`, `Magnetization` and `ParticleNumber` such that they are only given the `num_spatial_orbitals` information \"shortly before\" calling `second_q_ops()` (by extension, this will also fix #820)",
